From b0bc1c75f304099347cfc0cc880b556966b54138 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usama Arif <usama.arif@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 10:50:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sched/psi: skip irqtime accounting when no new irq time has
 elapsed

[ Backport of b0bc1c75f304 from 7.2 ]

psi_account_irqtime() bails out only when the irq-time delta is
negative. A delta of exactly zero still takes the seqcount write,
reads cpu_clock(), and walks the cgroup ancestor chain just to add 0
to every group's PSI_IRQ_FULL bucket.

The zero-delta case is common: it fires on every context switch that
crosses a PSI group on a CPU that has not serviced an interrupt
between the two switches. This tree has CONFIG_IRQ_TIME_ACCOUNTING=y
and CONFIG_PSI=y.

[ Adapted for OnePlus 6.1.141 OKI: irq time is still a per-cpu u64,
  not rq->psi_irq_time. Same delta <= 0 early return. ]

Signed-off-by: Usama Arif <usama.arif@linux.dev>
---
 kernel/sched/psi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/psi.c b/kernel/sched/psi.c
--- a/kernel/sched/psi.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/psi.c
@@ -979,7 +979,7 @@ void psi_account_irqtime(struct rq *rq, struct task_struct *curr, struct task_st
 
 	irq = irq_time_read(cpu);
 	psi_time =  &per_cpu(psi_irq_time, cpu);
 	delta = (s64)(irq - *psi_time);
-	if (delta < 0)
+	if (delta <= 0)
 		return;
 	*psi_time = irq;
 
